From: ZeroCD DVD support series
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: add READ DISC INFORMATION

READ DISC INFORMATION (opcode 0x51) is sent by some hosts (notably
Windows autorun and macOS disc mounting) to determine disc state,
erasability, and session/track counts.

We return a Standard Disc Information response indicating:
- Disc Status: Complete (finalized, not erasable)
- Last Session State: Complete
- Number of Sessions: 1
- First Track in Last Session: 1
- Last Track in Last Session: 1
- Disc Type: CD-ROM (0x00) -- even for DVD images; hosts check
the profile via GET CONFIGURATION, not disc type here
- No Disc ID, No OPC, No BCA

Data Block Type 0b00 (Standard Disc Information) is the only type
we support. Types 0b01 and 0b10 return INVALID FIELD IN CDB.

References: MMC-6 section 6.22 (READ DISC INFORMATION)

Signed-off-by: ZeroCD patch series
